# seccomp/filter.rs: the kernel structures, the list of the stopped calls and
# the BPF program. seccomp/notif.rs: the reply (the seam), the descriptors
# that the reply adds, the check of a notification id and the codec of a
# socket address. seccomp/mem.rs: the memory of the child. fdtable.rs: the
# table of the descriptors and the flow budget. seccomp/mod.rs: of it only
# the start of the program under the filter, the receive part of the loop
